          %h2#idea_and_motivation Idea and motivation
          %p
            Locale theory is one particular formulation of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/point-free+topology"} point-free topology
          %p
            A
            %em locale
            is, intuitively, like a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            that may or may not have enough
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/points"} points
            (or even any points at all). It contains things we call
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+subspaces"} open subspaces
            but there may or may not be enough points to distinguish between open subspaces. An open subspace in a locale can be regarded as conveying a bounded amount of information about the (hypothetical) points that it contains.
          %p
            For example, there is a locale of all
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/surjections"} surjections
            from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+numbers"} natural numbers
            (thought of as forming the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+space"} discrete space
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers"} real numbers
            (forming the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+line"} real line
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            = succeed ")." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locale+of+real+numbers"} locale of real numbers
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n\colon N
            and
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x\colon R
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            may be described as
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi N
                    %mo ↠
                    %mi R
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{f\colon N \twoheadrightarrow R \;|\; f(n) = x\}
            = succeed "\u2019" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∀
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi n
                    %mo ,
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ∃
                    %mo !
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \forall\, n,\; \exists!\, x,\; f(n) = x
            = succeed "\u2019," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∀
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ∃
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi n
                    %mo ,
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \forall\, x,\; \exists\, n,\; f(n) = x
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Elephant"} Elephant
          %p
            Every topological space can be regarded as a locale (with some lost information if the space is not
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sober+space"} sober
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+locale"} topological
            or
            %em spatial
            locales. Conversely, every locale induces a topology on its set of points, but sometimes a great deal of information is lost; in particular, there are many different locales whose set of points is
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/empty+set"} empty
          %p
            One motivation for locales is that since they take the notion of open subspace as basic, with the points (if any) being a derived notion, they are exactly what is needed to define
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaves"} sheaves
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/toposes"} toposes
            of sheaves is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+and+faithful+functor"} full and faithful functor
          %p
            Another advantage of locales is that they are better-behaved than topological spaces in alternative
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/foundations+of+mathematics"} foundations of mathematics
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+choice"} axiom of choice
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constructive+mathematics"} constructive mathematics
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internalization"} internal
            to an arbitrary
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [0,1]
            need not be
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+space"} compact
            %em locale
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [0,1]
            is always compact (in a suitable sense). It follows that the locale
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [0,1]
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            of real numbers, is not necessarily spatial. When it fails to be spatial, because there are “not enough real numbers,” the locale of real numbers is generally a better-behaved object than the topological space of real numbers.
          %h2#definitions Definitions
          %p
            Recall that a
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/frame"} frame
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partial+order"} poset
            with all
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/join"} joins
            and all finite
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/meet"} meets
            which satisfies the
            = succeed ":" do
              %em infinite distributive law
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ∧
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋁
                    %mi i
                  %msub
                    %mi y
                    %mi i
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋁
                    %mi i
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ∧
                  %msub
                    %mi y
                    %mi i
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \wedge (\bigvee_i y_i) = \bigvee_i (x\wedge y_i) .
          %p
            A
            %strong
              frame
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphism"} homomorphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi\colon A\to B
            is a function which preserves finite meets and arbitrary joins. Frames and frame homomorphisms form a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Frm"} Frm
          %p
            Note: By the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functor+theorem"} adjoint functor theorem
            (AFT) for posets, a frame also has all meets (at least assuming that it is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+set"} small set
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/predicative+mathematics"} impredicative quantification
            over it), but a frame homomorphism need not preserve them. Similarly, by the AFT, a frame is automatically a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Heyting+algebra"} Heyting algebra
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Heyting+implication"} Heyting implication
          %p
            By definition, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Locale"} Locale
            of
            %strong locales
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/opposite+category"} opposite
            of the category of frames
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Locale
                  %mo ≔
                  %msup
                    %mi Frm
                    %mi op
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Locale \coloneqq Frm^{op}
                  \\,.
          %p
            That is, a locale
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            “is” a frame, which we often write as
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi O
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O(X)
            and call “the frame of open subspaces of
            = succeed "\u201D," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+map"} continuous map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\colon X \to Y
            of locales is a frame homomorphism
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi O
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi O
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^*\colon O(Y) \to O(X)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lattice"} lattice
            satisfying a completeness condition), then this is an example of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/duality"} duality
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/space+and+quantity"} space and quantity
          %p
            It is also possible to think of a continuous map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\colon X \to Y
            as a map of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/posets"} posets
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi O
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi O
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_*\colon O(X) \to O(Y)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function"} function
            that preserves all
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/meets"} meets
            (and therefore is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monotone+function"} monotone
            and has a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi O
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi O
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^*\colon O(Y) \to O(X)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^*
            preserves all finite meets. This has the arrow pointing in the “right” direction, at the cost of a less direct definition. (In
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/predicative+mathematics"} predicative mathematics
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_*
            has a left adjoint; although since few locales even exist predicatively, we usually turn attention to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/base+of+a+locale"} bases
            of locales anyway.)
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              The map
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %mo :
                    %mi O
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi O
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_\ast: O(X) \to O(Y)
              is of course
              %em not
              the “direct image” along
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi u
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi O
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u \in O(X)
              to the join
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋁
                      %mrow
                        %mi v
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi O
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi Y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo :
                        %msup
                          %mi f
                          %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi v
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ≤
                        %mi u
                    %mi v
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bigvee_{v \in O(Y): f^\ast(v) \leq u} v
            %p
              For
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
              in
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+mathematics"} classical mathematics
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complementation"} complementation
              operator by
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ¬
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \neg
              and the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/interior"} interior
              operator by
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi int
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} int
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi u
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi int
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo ¬
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo ¬
                    %mi u
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_\ast(u) = int(\neg f(\neg u))
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              on the right denotes the ordinary set-theoretic direct image.
            %p
              Alternatively,
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi u
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_*(u)
              can also be described as the largest open subset of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
              whose preimage in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is a subset of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi u
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u
          %p
            The category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Locale
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Locale
            is naturally enhanced to a
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category"} 2-category
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition Definition
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category"} 2-category
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Locale"} Locale
              has
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  as
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/frames"} frames
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi O
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi X
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O(X)
              %li
                %p
                  as
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mi X
                        %mo →
                        %mi Y
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\colon X \to Y
                  frame homomorphisms
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi f
                            %mo *
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                          %mi O
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi Y
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo →
                          %mi O
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi X
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^*\colon O(Y) \to O(X)
              %li
                %p
                  a unique
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-morphism"} 2-morphism
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo ⇒
                        %mi g
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \Rightarrow g
                  whenever for all
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi U
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi O
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi Y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \in O(Y)
                  we have
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi f
                            %mo *
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi U
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ≤
                          %msup
                            %mi g
                            %mo *
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi U
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^*(U) \leq g^*(U)
          %p
            (See for instance
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a{:href => "#Johnstone"} Johnstone, C1.4, p. 514
          %p
            Since
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/parallel+morphisms"} parallel
            = succeed "-morphisms" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category"} 2-category
            is in fact a
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%281%2C2%29-category"} (1,2)-category
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poset"} Poset
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} enriched category
          %h2#Subsidiaries Subsidiary notions
          %h3#open_and_closed_subspaces Open and closed subspaces
          %p
            Given a locale
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi O
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O(X)
            are traditionally thought of as being the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+subspaces"} open subspaces
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            and are therefore called the
            %strong opens
            (or
            = succeed "," do
              %strong open subspaces
            = succeed "," do
              %strong open parts
            = succeed ")" do
              %strong open sublocales
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+subspaces"} closed subspaces
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            and call them the
            %strong closeds
            (or
            = succeed "," do
              %strong closed subspaces
            = succeed "," do
              %strong closed parts
            = succeed ")" do
              %strong closed sublocales
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/opposite+relation"} opposite
            containment relation is used; thus
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi O
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O(X)
            is the
            %strong frame of opens
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/opposite+poset"} opposite poset
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi O
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O(X)^{op}
            is the
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coframe"} coframe
              of closeds
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p
            An open subspace may be thought of as a potentially
            %em verifiable
            property of a hypothetical point of the space
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intersection"} intersection
            of two open subspaces by verifying both properties, and we may verify the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/union"} union
            of any family of open subspaces by verifying at least one of them; but it may not necessarily make sense to verify the intersection of infinitely many open subspaces, because this would require us to do an infinite amount of work. (The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/meet"} meet
            of an arbitrary family of open subspaces does exist, but the construction is impredicative, and it does not match the meet within the lattice of all subspaces.)
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Morgan+duality"}> Dually
            , a closed subspace may be thought of as a potentially
            %em refutable
            property. Thus we may refute the union of two closed subspaces by refuting both of them, and we may refute the intersection of any family of closed subspaces by refuting at least one of them; but it may not necessarily make sense to refute the union of infinitely many closed subspaces. (Again, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/join"} join
            of an arbitrary family of closed subspaces does not work right.)
          %p
            If one views an element of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi O
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O(X)
            as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subspace"} subspace
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi O
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O(X)
            to the lattice of all subspaces of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sublocale"} sublocale
            for further discussion.
          %h3#points Points
          %p
            As a locale, the
            %strong
              abstract
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/point"} point
            is the locale
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
            whose frame of opens is the frame of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/truth+values"} truth values
            (classically
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mo ⊥
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mo ⊤
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{\bot \lt \top\}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object"} terminal object
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Locale
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Locale
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\colon X \to 1
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo ⊤
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mo ⊤
                    %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^*(\top) = \top_X
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo ⊥
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mo ⊥
                    %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^*(\bot) = \bot_X
            (and most generally
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋁
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊤
                      %mi X
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^*(p) = \bigvee \{\top_X \;|\; p\}
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋁
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mo ⊤
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p = \bigvee \{\top \;|\; p\}
          %p
            Given a locale
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %strong
              concrete
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/point+of+a+locale"} point
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            may be defined in any of the following equivalent ways:
          %ol
            %li
              A point of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+map"} continuous map
              = succeed ";" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mn 1
                      %mo →
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\colon 1 \to X
            %li
              Unravelling this in terms of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi O
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi O
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^*\colon O(X) \to O(1)
              and viewing this as a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/characteristic+function"} characteristic function
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/completely+prime+filter"} completely prime filter
              in
              = succeed ";" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi O
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O(X)
            %li
              Unravelling (1) in terms of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi f
                        %mo *
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi O
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mi O
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_*\colon O(1) \to O(X)
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/excluded+middle"} excluded middle
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi f
                        %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo ⊥
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_*(\bot)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prime+element"} prime element
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi O
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O(X)
          %p
            Definition (3) is simpler than (2), being an element of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi O
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O(X)
            satisfying a finitary condition rather than a subset of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi O
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O(X)
            satisfying an infinitary condition. However, it doesn't work in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constructive+mathematics"} constructive mathematics
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#CategoryOfLocales Categories of internal locales
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              The category
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Locale"} Locale
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (E)
              of locales
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internalization"} internal to
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              is equivalent to the category of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localic+geometric+morphisms"} localic geometric morphisms
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Sh
                      %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh_{E}(\Sigma) \to E
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Topos"} Topos
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Locale
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Topos
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi E
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi loc
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Locale(E) \simeq (Topos/E)_{loc}
                    \\,.
          %p
            See
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localic+geometric+morphism"} localic geometric morphism
            for more.
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              For every locale
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Locale
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Sh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Locale(Sh(X))
              of locales internal to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf+topos"} sheaf topos
              over
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is equivalent to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/overcategory"} overcategory
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Locale
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Locale/X
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℐ
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi Locale
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi X
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo ≃
                    %mi Locale
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Sh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathcal{I}\colon Locale/X \stackrel{\simeq}{\to} Locale(Sh(X))
                    \\,.
          %p
            This appears as
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Johnstone"} Johnstone, theorem C1.6.3
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              For every morphism of locales
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi Y
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\colon Y \to X
              the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf+topos"} sheaf topos
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Sh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh(Y)
              is equivalent as a topos over
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Sh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh(X)
              to the topos
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Sh
                      %mrow
                        %mi Sh
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℐ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh_{Sh(X)}(\mathcal{I}(Y))
              of internal sheaves over the internal locale
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℐ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Sh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{I}(Y) \in Sh(X)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Sh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi Sh
                      %mrow
                        %mi Sh
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℐ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Sh(Y) \simeq Sh_{Sh(X)}(\mathcal{I}(Y))
                    \\,.
          %p
            This appears as
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Johnstone"} Johnstone, scholium C1.6.4
          %h3#RelationToTopologicalSpaces Relation to topological spaces
          %p
            Every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            has a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/frame+of+opens"} frame of opens
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi O
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O(X)
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_L
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+function"} continuous function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\colon X \to Y
            between topological spaces, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/preimage"} inverse image
            map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi O
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi O
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^{-1}\colon O(Y) \to O(X)
            is a frame homomorphism, so
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            induces a continuous map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mi L
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mi L
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi Y
                    %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_L\colon X_L \to Y_L
            of locales. Thus we have a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi L
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-)_L\colon
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo →
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \to
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Loc"} Locale
          %p
            Conversely, if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is any locale, we define a
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/point"} point
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            to be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+map"} continuous map
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1 \to X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object"} terminal
            locale, which can be defined as the locale
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mn 1
                    %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1_L
            corresponding to the terminal space. Explicitly, we have
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi O
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O(1) = P(1)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/powerset"} powerset
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
            (the initial frame, the set of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/truth+values"} truth values
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2
            classically or in a
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Boolean+topos"} Boolean topos
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi O
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O(X) \to P(1)
            is determined by the preimage of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
            (the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/true"} true
            truth value), a point can also be described more explicitly as a
            = succeed ":" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/completely+prime+filter"} completely prime filter
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi O
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O(X)
            such that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in F
            (
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            denotes the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/top+element"} top element
            of
            = succeed ")," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi O
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O(X)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo ,
                  %mi V
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U,V \in F
            then
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo ∩
                    %mi V
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \cap V \in F
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋃
                    %mi i
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi i
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bigcup_i U_i \in F
            then
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi i
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_i \in F
            for some
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
          %p
            The elements of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi O
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O(X)
            induce a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+structure"} topology
            on the set of points of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            in an obvious way, thereby giving rise to a topological space
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_P
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\colon X \to Y
            of locales induces a continuous map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mi P
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mi P
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi Y
                    %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_P\colon X_P \to Y_P
            of spaces, so we have another functor
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi P
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi Locale
                  %mo →
                  %mi Top
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-)_P\colon Locale \to Top
            \.
          %p
            One finds that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-)_L
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
            to
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-)_P
          %p
            In fact, this is an
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/idempotent+adjunction"} idempotent adjunction
          #TopLocAdjunction.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_4 Proposition
            %p
              The categories
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
              and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Loc"} Locale
              of locales are related by an
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/idempotent+adjunction"} idempotent adjunction
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi L
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi Top
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %munderover
                      %mo ⊥
                      %munder
                        %mo ⟵
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %msub
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mi P
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %msub
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mi L
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi Locale
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (
                    (-)_L \dashv (-)_P
                    )
                    \\colon
                    Top
                    \\;
                    \\underoverset
                    {\underset{(-)_P}{\longleftarrow}}
                    {\overset{(-)_L}{\longrightarrow}}
                    {\bot}
                    \\;
                    Locale
                    \\,.
          %p
            This appears for instance as (
            %a{:href => "#MacLaneMoerdijk"}> MacLaneMoerdijk, theorem IX.3 1
            ) or as (
            %a{:href => "#Johnstone"}> Johnstone, lemma C.1.2.2
            ).
          %p
            Therefore the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction"} adjunction
            restricts to an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalence
            between the fixed subcategories on either side.
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ≅
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mrow
                        %mi L
                        %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \cong X_{L P}
              is called
              = succeed "." do
                %strong
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sober+space"} sober
            %p
              A locale with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ≅
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mrow
                        %mi P
                        %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \cong X_{P L}
              is called
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spatial+locale"} spatial
              or
              = succeed ";" do
                %strong topological
              = succeed "." do
                %strong enough points
          %p
            see also MO
            %a{:href => "http://math.stackexchange.com/a/1904289/58526"} here
          .num_cor
            %h6#corollary Corollary
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction"} adjunction
              from prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TopLocAdjunction"}
              exhibits
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sober+topological+spaces"} sober topological spaces
              as a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coreflective+subcategory"} coreflective subcategory
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Locale"} Locale
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi L
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi SoberTop
                    %munderover
                      %mo ⊥
                      %munder
                        %mo ←
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %msub
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mi P
                      %mover
                        %mo ↪
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %msub
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mi L
                    %mi Locale
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (
                    (-)_L \dashv (-)_P
                    )
                    \\colon
                    SoberTop
                    \\underoverset
                    {\underset{(-)_P}{\leftarrow}}
                    {\overset{(-)_L}{\hookrightarrow}}
                    {\bot}
                    Locale
            %p
              and this restricts to an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalence of categories
              between the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
              of locales with enough points, and that of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sober+topological+spaces"} sober topological spaces
          %p
            This appears for instance as (
            %a{:href => "#MacLaneMoerdijk"}> MacLaneMoerdijk, corollary IX.3 4
            ).
          %p Consequently, we often identify a sober topological space and the corresponding topological locale.
          %h3#RelationToToposes Relation to toposes – localic reflection
          %p
            The notion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+topos"} Grothendieck topos
            can be seen as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorification"} categorification
            of the notion of locale, by relating both notions to the notion of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/total+category"} lex totality
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_5 Proposition
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/poset"} poset
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/frame"} frame
              if and only if the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+embedding"} Yoneda embedding
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi P
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mn 2
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi P
                          %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    y \colon P \to \mathbf{2}^{P^{op}}
            %p
              has a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exact+functor"} left exact
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{2}
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/truth+values"} truth values
              is the base of enrichment for posets seen as
              = succeed ".)" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+categories"} enriched categories
          %p
            The analogous result for toposes involves a bit of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set+theory"} set theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ZFC"} ZFC
            plus the existence of a
            %span.newWikiWord
              strong inaccessible cardinal
              %a{:href => "/nlab/new/strong+inaccessible+cardinal"} ?
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Categories+for+the+Working+Mathematician"} Categories for the Working Mathematician
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moderate+category"} moderate
            if its set of morphisms has size
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
            is moderate.
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_6 Proposition
            %p
              (
              %a{:href => "#Street"}> Street
              )
            %p
              A moderate
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+small+category"} locally small category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+topos"} Grothendieck topos
              if and only if the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+embedding"} Yoneda embedding
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi Set
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi C
                          %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y \colon C \to Set^{C^{op}}
            %p
              has a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+exact+functor"} left exact
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
          %p
            These results emphasize frames/toposes as algebras, where the morphisms are left exact left adjoints. The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+adjoints"} right adjoints
            to such morphisms are called
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+morphism"} geometric morphisms
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spaces"} spaces
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#JT"} Joyal and Tierney
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/frame+of+opens"} frame of opens
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi O
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O(X)
            corresponding to a locale
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is naturally a
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              Given a locale
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/frame+of+opens"} frame of opens
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi O
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O(X)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo →
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{U_i \to U\}
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi O
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O(X)
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cover"} cover
              if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/join"} join
              of the
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_i
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mo ∨
                      %mi i
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    U = \vee_i U_i
                    \\,.
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_7 Proposition
            %p
              This defines a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coverage"} coverage
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi O
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O(X)
              and hence makes it a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
          %p
            See for instance (
            %a{:href => "#MacLaneMoerdijk"}> MacLaneMoerdijk, section 5
            ).
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_4 Definition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              a locale, write
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Sh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≔
                    %mi Sh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi O
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Sh(X) \coloneqq Sh(O(X))
            %p
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf+topos"} sheaf topos
              over the category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi O
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O(X)
              equipped with the above canonical structure of a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
          %p
            Write
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Topos"} Topos
            for the category of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+toposes"} Grothendieck toposes
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+morphisms"} geometric morphisms
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_8 Proposition
            %p
              This construction defines a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+and+faithful+functor"} full and faithful functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Sh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh(-) :
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Locale"} Locale
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo →
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \to
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Topos"} Topos
          %p
            This appears for instance as
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#MacLaneMoerdijk"} MacLaneMoerdijk, section IX.5 prop 2
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_5 Definition
            %p
              A topos in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/image"} image
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Sh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi Locale
                    %mo →
                    %mi Topos
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh(-)\colon Locale \to Topos
              is called a
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localic+topos"} localic topos
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_9 Proposition
            %p
              The functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Sh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi Locale
                    %mo →
                    %mi Topos
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh(-)\colon Locale \to Topos
              has a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi Topos
                    %mo →
                    %mi Locale
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    L\colon Topos \to Locale
            %p
              given by sending a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℰ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
              to the locale that is formally dual to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/frame"} frame
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subobjects"} subobjects
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object"} terminal object
              of
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℰ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi O
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℰ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≔
                    %msub
                      %mi Sub
                      %mi ℰ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    O(L(\mathcal{E})) \coloneqq Sub_{\mathcal{E}}(*)
                    \\,.
          %p
            This appears for instance as
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#MacLaneMoerdijk"} MacLaneMoerdijk, section IX.5 prop 3
          %p
            The functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            here is also called
            = succeed "." do
              %strong localic reflection
          %p
            In summary this means that locales form a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflective+subcategory"} reflective subcategory
            of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Topos"} Topos
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Locale
                  %mover
                    %mo ↪
                    %mover
                      %mo ←
                      %mi L
                  %mi Topos
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Locale \stackrel{\overset{L}{\leftarrow}}{\hookrightarrow}
                  Topos
                  \\,.
          %p
            In fact this is even a genuine
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+sub-2-category"} full sub-2-category
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_10 Proposition
            %p
              For all
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ∈
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X,Y \in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Locale"} Locale
              the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-functor"} 2-functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Sh
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh\colon
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Locale"} Locale
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo →
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \to
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Topos"} Topos
              induces an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalence of categories
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Sh
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi Locale
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo ≃
                    %mi Topos
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Sh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Sh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Sh\colon Locale(X,Y) \stackrel{\simeq}{\to} Topos(Sh(X), Sh(Y))
                    \\,.
          %p
            This appears as (
            %a{:href => "#Johnstone"}> Johnstone, prop. C1.4.5
            ).
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_11 Proposition
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/poset+of+subobjects"} poset of subobjects
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Sub
                      %mi ℰ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sub_{\mathcal{E}}(*)
              of the terminal object of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℰ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
              is equivalent to the full
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subcategory"} subcategory
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi τ
                      %mrow
                        %mo ≤
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℰ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tau_{\leq -1}(\mathcal{E})
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℰ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
              on the
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-1)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/truncated"} truncated
              objects of
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Sub
                      %mi ℰ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi τ
                      %mrow
                        %mo ≤
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mi ℰ
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Sub_{\mathcal{E}}(*) \simeq \tau_{\leq -1} \mathcal{E}
                    \\,.
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28-1%29-truncated"} (-1)-truncated
              sheaf
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is one whose values over any object are either the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28-2%29-groupoid"} singleton set
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/empty+set"} empty set
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∈
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mo *
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ∅
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo =
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi Set
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    X(X) \in \{*, \emptyset\} = \subset Set
                    \\,.
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monomorphism"} monomorphism
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaves"} sheaves
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} natural transformation
              that is degreewise a monomorphism of sets (an
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injection"} injection
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subobjects"} subobjects
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object"} terminal
              sheaf (that assigns the singleton set to every object) are precisely the sheaves of this form.
          %p
            We may think of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/frame"} frame
            as a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+%280%2C1%29-topos"} Grothendieck (0,1)-topos
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+toposes"} Grothendieck toposes
            onto
            = succeed "-toposes" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (0,1)
            = succeed "-truncation:" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-1)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            a locale,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Sh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh(X)
            the corresponding
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localic+topos"} localic topos
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℰ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
            any Grothendieck topos we have a natural equivalence
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Gr
                  %mn 1
                  %mi Topos
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℰ
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Sh
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi Gr
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi Topos
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi τ
                    %mrow
                      %mo ≤
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mi ℰ
                  %mo ,
                  %mi O
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Gr1Topos( \mathcal{E},  Sh X) \simeq Gr(0,1)Topos(\tau_{\leq -1} \mathcal{E}, O(X))
          %p which is
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi Frame
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi O
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi Sub
                    %mi ℰ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi Locale
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi L
                  %mi ℰ
                  %mo ,
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\cdots \simeq Frame(O(X), Sub_{\mathcal{E}}(*))
                  \\simeq
                  Locale(L \mathcal{E} , X)
                  \\,.
          %p
            This is a small part of a pattern in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+topos+theory"} higher topos theory
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-localic+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} n-localic (∞,1)-topos
          %h2#Examples Examples
          %h3#general_topology General topology
          %p
            As explained above, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
            to locales provides a very large collection of examples. When restricted to
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sober+topological+spaces"} sober topological spaces
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fully+faithful+functor"} fully faithful
            and its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/essential+images"} essential images
            consists of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spatial+locales"} spatial locales
          %p
            Without the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom"} axiom
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/excluded+middle"} excluded middle
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/the+locale+of+real+numbers"} the locale of real numbers
            or
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cantor+space"} Cantor space
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spatial+locale"} spatial
          %p Naturally, one is interested in examples of locales that are not spatial, and a few are given below.
          %h3#ExamplesMeasureTheory Measure theory
          %p
            An amazing feature of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointfree+topology"} pointfree topology
            is that it contains not only point-set
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/general+topology"} general topology
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/measure+theory"} measure theory
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
          %p
            Specifically, recall from the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/duality+between+geometry+and+algebra"} duality between geometry and algebra
            that various categories of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+algebras"} commutative algebras
            are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/opposite+category"} contravariantly
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalent
            to certain corresponding categories of spaces. The category of algebras relevant for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/measure+theory"} measure theory
            is the category of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+von+Neumann+algebras"} commutative von Neumann algebras
            and ultraweakly continuous *-homomorphisms; it is widely accepted that dropping the commutativity condition and passing to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/opposite+category"} opposite category
            yields the correct category of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/noncommutative+measurable+spaces"} noncommutative measurable spaces
          %p
            The category of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+von+Neumann+algebras"} commutative von Neumann algebras
            is contravariantly
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalent
            to several other categories:
          %ul
            %li
              %p compact strictly localizable enhanced measurable spaces and measurable maps;
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hyperstonean+topological+spaces"} hyperstonean topological spaces
                and
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+maps"} open maps
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hyperstonean+locales"} hyperstonean locales
                and
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+maps"} open maps
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/measurable+locales"} measurable locales
                and maps of locales.
          %p
            The last category is particularly interesting: it is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locales"} locales
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/measure+theory"} measure theory
            embeds into pointfree topology, which means that methods and results from pointfree topology can be used right away in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/measure+theory"} measure theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
            and point-set
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/measurable+spaces"} measurable spaces
          %p
            With the exception of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+locales"} discrete locales
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/measurable+locales"} measurable locales
            are
            %em never
            spatial, and in fact do not have any points other than those in its atomic (discrete) part, which splits off as a coproduct summand.
          %h3#intersections_of_dense_sublocales Intersections of dense sublocales
          %p
            Another important source of nonspatial sublocales is given by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intersections"} intersections
            (of arbitrary cardinality) of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dense+sublocales"} dense sublocales
          %p
            Again, in contrast to the point-set setting, where the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Baire+category+theorem"} Baire category theorem
            identifies the rather restrictive conditions under which the intersection of dense topological subspaces is again dense, in the pointfree setting arbitrary intersections of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dense+sublocales"} dense sublocales
            are always dense.
          %p
            In particular, one can intersection all
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dense+sublocales"} dense sublocales
            of a given
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locale"} locale
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/double+negation+sublocale"} double negation sublocale
          %p
            But there are other interesting examples. Connecting to
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/measure+theory"} measure theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/valuation"} valuation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ν
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nu
            on a given
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locale"} locale
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            and take the intersection of all
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sublocales"} sublocales
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            such that
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ν
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi ν
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nu(S)=\nu(1)
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                The notion of locale may be identified with that of a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+topos"} Grothendieck
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%280%2C1%29-topos"} (0,1)-topos
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Heyting+algebra"} Heyting algebra
                for more on this.
            %li
              %p
                An
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ionad"} ionad
                is to a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
                as a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+topos"} Grothendieck topos
                is to a
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locale"} locale
            %li
              %p
                A
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+object"} group object
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internalization"} internal
                to locales or an
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+groupoid"} internal groupoid
                in locales is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localic+group"} localic group
                or
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localic+groupoid"} localic groupoid
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/positive+locale"}> positive locale
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+positive+locale"} locally positive locale
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/premetric+locale"}> premetric locale
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metric+locale"} metric locale
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/preuniform+locale"}> preuniform locale
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/uniform+locale"} uniform locale
          %p
            There is also a notion of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+locale"} internal locale
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+site"} internal site
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"}> topological space
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+locale"} topological locale
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ionad"} ionad
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/profinite+space"}> profinite space
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/profinite+reflection"} profinite reflection
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localic+homotopy+theory"} localic homotopy theory
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+hyperdoctrine"} geometric hyperdoctrine
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coherent+locale"} coherent locale
          %h2#references References
          %p An early paper, containing much of the basic theory, and in which the term “locale” is introduced:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+R.+Isbell"}> John R. Isbell
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Atomless Parts of Spaces
              %strong 31
              (1972) 5–32 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.7146/math.scand.a-11409"}> doi:10.7146/math.scand.a-11409
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            An introduction to and survey of the use of locales instead of topological spaces (“
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/point-free+topology"}> point-free topology
            ”):
          %ul
            %li#Johnstone83
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Johnstone"}> Peter Johnstone
              \:
              = succeed ";" do
                %em The point of pointless topology
              %strong 8
              1 (1983) 41-53 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://www.ams.org/bull/1983-08-01/S0273-0979-1983-15080-2/home.html"} ams:1983-08-01/S0273-0979-1983-15080-2
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "http://projecteuclid.org/euclid.bams/1183550014"} euclid:bams/1183550014
              %blockquote
                %p
                  (advertised as the “trailer” for
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "#Johnstone82"} Johnston 1982
          %p
            that develops, among other things, much of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/general+topology"} general topology
            entirely with the notion of locales used in place of that of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
          %p
            Monographs on locales and
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointfree+topology"} pointfree topology
          %ul
            %li#Johnstone82
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Johnstone"}> Peter Johnstone
                \:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stone+Spaces"} Stone Spaces
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 3
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.cambridge.org/de/academic/subjects/mathematics/logic-categories-and-sets/stone-spaces?format=PB&isbn=9780521337793"} ISBN:9780521337793
            %li#PicadoPultr12
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jorge+Picado"}> Jorge Picado
                ,
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ales%CC%8C+Pultr"} Aleš Pultr
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Frames+and+Locales"} Frames and Locales
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-0348-0154-6"} doi:10.1007/978-3-0348-0154-6
          %p Other textbook accounts:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Francis+Borceux"}> Francis Borceux
                , volume 3, chapter 1 of
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Handbook+of+Categorical+Algebra"} Handbook of Categorical Algebra
            %li#Johnstone
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Johnstone"}> Peter Johnstone
                , part C (volume 2)
                = succeed "." do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Elephant"} Sketches of an elephant: a topos theory compendium
            %li#MacLaneMoerdijk
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Saunders+MacLane"}> Saunders MacLane
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ieke+Moerdijk"} Ieke Moerdijk
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sheaves+in+Geometry+and+Logic"} Sheaves in Geometry and Logic
            %li
              %p
                Jorge Picado &amp; Aleš Pultr (2012).
                = succeed "." do
                  %em Frames and Locales: Topology without points
                %a{:href => "http://www.mat.uc.pt/%7Epicado/publicat/bookpage.html"} Web page
                (with preface, contents, and errata).
          %p and
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Steve+Vickers"}> Steve Vickers
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Topology via logic
          %p
            where the latter develops topology from the point of view of its
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+logic"} internal logic
          %p An introductory survey is
          %ul
            %li
              Jorge Picado, Aleš Pultr, Anna Tozzi,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Locales
              %em Categorical Foundations
              , CUP 2004. (
              %a{:href => "http://www.mat.uc.pt/~picado/publicat/Chapter2.pdf"}> draft
              )
          %p See also
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/eom"}> eom
              ,
              %em
                %a{:href => "https://www.encyclopediaofmath.org/index.php/Locale"} Locale
          %p Lex totality is the subject of an article of Street,
          %ul
            %li#Street
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ross+Street"}> Ross Street
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Notions of Topos
          %p The connection between locales and toposes via lex totality plays a tacit role throughout the influential monograph
          %ul
            %li#JT
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andr%C3%A9+Joyal"} André Joyal
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Myles+Tierney"} Myles Tierney
              = succeed "," do
                %em An Extension of the Galois Theory of Grothendieck
          %p A basic introduction to locale theory can be found in section 1 of
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ingo+Blechschmidt"}> Ingo Blechschmidt
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Generalized spaces for constructive algebra
              = succeed ")" do
